                ("PHY101", "Vectors and Scalars", "If the sum of two unit vectors is also a unit vector, what is the magnitude of their difference?", "1", "√2", "√3", "2", "C", "Let the unit vectors be a and b. |a| = 1, |b| = 1. We are given |a + b| = 1. Squaring both sides: |a|² + |b|² + 2|a||b|cos(θ) = 1. So, 1 + 1 + 2(1)(1)cos(θ) = 1, which gives 2cos(θ) = -1, or cos(θ) = -1/2. The magnitude of their difference is |a - b| = √(|a|² + |b|² - 2|a||b|cos(θ)) = √(1 + 1 - 2(1)(1)(-1/2)) = √(2 + 1) = √3."),
