                ("PHY101", "Vectors and Scalars", "If the dot product of two non-zero vectors is equal to the magnitude of their cross product, what is the angle between the vectors?", "30°", "45°", "60°", "90°", "B", "We are given A • B = |A × B|. This means |A||B|cos(θ) = |A||B|sin(θ). Since the vectors are non-zero, we can divide by |A||B| to get cos(θ) = sin(θ). This implies tan(θ) = 1. The angle whose tangent is 1 is 45°."),
                ("PHY101", "Vectors and Scalars", "A vector V is directed at an angle of 120° counterclockwise from the positive x-axis. If its y-component is 10√3, what is its x-component?", "-10", "10", "-10√3", "20", "A", "The y-component is Vy = V sin(120°) = V (√3/2). We are given Vy = 10√3. So, V (√3/2) = 10√3, which means V = 20. The x-component is Vx = V cos(120°) = 20 (-1/2) = -10."),
