                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "Which of the following correctly represents a genotype?", "Tall plant", "Green eyes", "TT or Tt", "Height of 180 cm", "C", "Explanation: Genotype refers to the genetic makeup, represented by allele combinations such as TT or Tt"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "In a monohybrid cross, the phenotypic ratio of the F2 generation (complete dominance) is:", "1:1", "3:1", "9:3:3:1", "2:1", "B", "Explanation: A typical monohybrid cross yields a 3:1 phenotypic ratio in the F2 generation"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "What is the law of segregation?", "Genes from different traits assort independently", "Alleles separate during gamete formation", "Dominant alleles always mask recessive ones", "Genes mutate during inheritance", "B", "Explanation: The law of segregation states that allele pairs separate so each gamete carries one allele"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "Which of the following best describes homozygous condition?", "Two different alleles for a gene", "One allele present", "Two identical alleles for a gene", "Multiple genes interacting", "C", "Explanation: Homozygous means having two identical alleles (e.g., TT or tt)"),
