                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "Which structure carries genetic information in eukaryotic cells?", "Ribosomes", "Mitochondria", "Chromosomes", "Golgi apparatus", "C", "Explanation: Chromosomes in the nucleus carry genetic information in the form of DNA"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "Variation caused by environmental factors alone is called:", "Genetic variation", "Continuous variation", "Environmental variation", "Discontinuous variation", "C", "Explanation: Environmental variation arises from external influences like diet and climate"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "Which of the following is an example of genetic variation?", "Skin tanning", "Height increase due to nutrition", "Blood group differences", "Muscle growth from exercise", "C", "Explanation: Blood group is determined genetically and not influenced by environment"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "In Mendelian genetics, a dominant allele is one that:", "Is always more common", "Masks the expression of another allele", "Is weaker than recessive allele", "Disappears in F1 generation", "B", "Explanation: A dominant allele expresses itself even in the presence of a recessive allele"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "Which base pairing rule is correct in DNA?", "A pairs with C", "G pairs with T", "A pairs with T", "C pairs with A", "C", "Explanation: Adenine pairs with thymine, while guanine pairs with cytosine"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "What is the function of chromosomes during cell division?", "Produce energy", "Store lipids", "Ensure accurate distribution of DNA", "Synthesize proteins", "C", "Explanation: Chromosomes ensure genetic material is accurately passed to daughter cells"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "Which of the following best explains discontinuous variation?", "Traits show a range of values", "Traits fall into distinct categories", "Traits are influenced only by environment", "Traits are not inherited", "B", "Explanation: Discontinuous variation involves distinct categories like blood groups"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "A test cross is used to determine:", "Phenotype of an organism", "Genotype of a dominant individual", "Chromosome number", "DNA structure", "B", "Explanation: A test cross reveals whether a dominant phenotype is homozygous or heterozygous"),
                ("BIO101", "Genetics", "Which molecule is directly responsible for inheritance?", "Protein", "RNA", "DNA", "Lipids", "C", "Explanation: DNA carries genetic information that is passed from parents to offspring"),
